DampingRatio

The Formula for the Damping Ratio

The damping ratio expresses whether a mass-spring-damper system is underdamped, critically damped, or overdamped.

\zeta = \frac{c}{2\sqrt{km}}

where:

\zeta [var. scal. DampingRatio] is the damping ratio
c [var. scal. DampingCoefficient] is the damping coefficient
m [var. scal. Mass] is the mass
k [var. scal. SpringConstant] is the spring constant

